  <main>
    <div class="category">Fantasy Football • Power Rankings</div>
    <h1 class="article-title">2026 Preseason Power Rankings: Championship Favorites, Red Flags and Complete Roster Breakdowns</h1>

    <div class="author-bar">
      <div class="author-img">BR</div>
      <div class="author-info">
        <div class="author-name">B/R Scouting Department</div>
        <div class="date">Updated August 28, 2026 • 6 min read</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="lead-paragraph">
      Twelve managers. Twelve draft strategies. Zero room for excuses. With kickoff right around the corner, we dissect who built a juggernaut and who is already looking toward the 2027 draft.
    </div>

    <div class="rank-card">
      <div class="rank-header">
        <h2 class="rank-title">🥇 1. Michael's Magnificent Team — Michael</h2>
        <span class="projection-badge">PROJ: 146.3 PTS</span>
      </div>
      <div class="player-roster">Ja'Marr Chase • Justin Jefferson • A.J. Brown • Breece Hall • Ashton Jeanty</div>
      <p class="rank-analysis">Michael didn't draft a fantasy team. He drafted a Pro Bowl roster.</p>
      <p class="rank-analysis">The only thing more questionable than his loaded roster is the fact that he swings a golf club exclusively left-handed. Nobody saw that coming.</p>
      <div class="verdict">Verdict: Undisputed Championship Favorite.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="rank-card">
      <div class="rank-header">
        <h2 class="rank-title">🥈 2. CeeDeez Nuts — Reese</h2>
        <span class="projection-badge">PROJ: 140.4 PTS</span>
      </div>
      <div class="player-roster">Mahomes • Achane • Jacobs • Amon-Ra • Higgins</div>
      <p class="rank-analysis">A terrifying core. Reese has a legitimate shot at the title. But can he manage a newborn, a garden, AND fantasy football?</p>
      <p class="rank-analysis"><em>Analyst prediction:</em> At least one crucial lineup decision will be missed because “the baby needed something.”</p>
      <div class="verdict">Verdict: Championship Threat (Pending Nap Schedules).</div>
    </div>

    <div class="rank-card">
      <div class="rank-header">
        <h2 class="rank-title">🥉 3. Drewbacca — Drew</h2>
        <span class="projection-badge">PROJ: ~140.0 PTS</span>
      </div>
      <div class="player-roster">Purdy • Bijan • Burden • Egbuka • McBride • Herbert</div>
      <p class="rank-analysis">One of the strongest rosters in the league. Unfortunately, Drew is also the commissioner. Every suspicious waiver move, questionable trade, and favorable ruling will immediately be investigated.</p>
      <blockquote class="pullquote">
        “I don't think Drew is cheating.”
        <span>— Drew</span>
      </blockquote>
      <div class="verdict">Verdict: Championship Contender Under Federal Investigation.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="rank-card">
      <div class="rank-header">
        <h2 class="rank-title">4. JoeMama — Daniel</h2>
        <span class="projection-badge">PROJ: 136.1 PTS</span>
      </div>
      <p class="rank-analysis">A solid roster with legitimate playoff potential. Unfortunately, Daniel has one obstacle he simply cannot overcome:</p>
      <p class="rank-analysis">He will never be as handsome as his older brother.</p>
      <div class="verdict">Verdict: Playoff contender.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="rank-card">
      <div class="rank-header">
        <h2 class="rank-title">5. Philupataco — Phil</h2>
        <span class="projection-badge">PROJ: 136.2 PTS</span>
      </div>
      <div class="player-roster">Christian McCaffrey • CeeDee Lamb • Malik Nabers • Trey McBride</div>
      <p class="rank-analysis">Phil brings an impressive fantasy football résumé. Unfortunately for him, nobody cares about the past. This is a new league, and the rest of the managers are ready to humble him.</p>
      <div class="verdict">Verdict: Dark-horse championship threat.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="rank-card">
      <div class="rank-header">
        <h2 class="rank-title">6. Levi's Loud Team — Levi</h2>
        <span class="projection-badge">PROJ: 135.0 PTS</span>
      </div>
      <div class="player-roster">Stafford • Gibbs • Derrick Henry • Garrett Wilson • Kyle Pitts</div>
      <p class="rank-analysis">A respectable roster. But nobody is talking about the roster—they're talking about Phil. Sources report Levi has developed what can only be described as a “deep admiration” for Phil.</p>
      <div class="verdict">Verdict: Levi, just tell him.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="rank-card">
      <div class="rank-header">
        <h2 class="rank-title">7. FoosGoneWild — Gordies</h2>
        <span class="projection-badge">PROJ: 132.3 PTS</span>
      </div>
      <div class="player-roster">Josh Allen • Hampton • Kyren Williams • Nico Collins • D.J. Moore</div>
      <p class="rank-analysis">Sneaky good team. Unfortunately, Gordies can't see worth a damn. While everyone else is studying matchups, Gordies is waiting for the audio-description version of the ESPN app.</p>
      <div class="verdict">Verdict: Sneaky contender.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="rank-card">
      <div class="rank-header">
        <h2 class="rank-title">8. Touch Down Syndrome — Chris</h2>
        <span class="projection-badge">PROJ: 131.4 PTS</span>
      </div>
      <div class="player-roster">Jaxson Dart • Saquon Barkley • A.J. Brown • JSN • Travis Kelce</div>
      <p class="rank-analysis">Could be brilliant. Could be an absolute disaster. Chris looks like he would fit into plenty of fantasy leagues—football just isn't one of them.</p>
      <div class="verdict">Verdict: Volatile Wildcard.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="rank-card">
      <div class="rank-header">
        <h2 class="rank-title">9. Darek's Driven Team — Darek</h2>
        <span class="projection-badge">PROJ: 129.8 PTS</span>
      </div>
      <div class="player-roster">Lamar Jackson • Rashee Rice • Etienne • Judkins</div>
      <p class="rank-analysis">Not a bad roster, but Darek may have confused fantasy football with golf. He's good at one. This isn't it.</p>
      <div class="verdict">Verdict: Better Luck on the Back Nine.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="rank-card">
      <div class="rank-header">
        <h2 class="rank-title">10. Donowitz — Donovan</h2>
        <span class="projection-badge">PROJ: 128.9 PTS</span>
      </div>
      <p class="rank-analysis">Jalen Hurts gives Donovan a strong foundation, but his biggest weapon might be his temper.</p>
      <blockquote class="pullquote">
        “A red-headed stepchild with anger issues who has somehow been given access to the waiver wire.”
        <span>— League Scout Report</span>
      </blockquote>
      <p class="rank-analysis">The question isn't whether Donovan can win. It's whether he can lose without declaring war on the league.</p>
      <div class="verdict">Verdict: High Threat Level (Group Chat Danger).</div>
    </div>

    <div class="rank-card">
      <div class="rank-header">
        <h2 class="rank-title">11. Cooking Up Wins — Frank</h2>
        <span class="projection-badge">PROJ: 127.2 PTS</span>
      </div>
      <div class="player-roster">Maye • Olave • Sutton • Bowers • Addison</div>
      <p class="rank-analysis">There are some intriguing pieces here. Unfortunately, Frank's fantasy history hasn't exactly cooked up many wins. Maybe he should stick to the kitchen.</p>
      <div class="verdict">Verdict: Kitchen Disaster.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="rank-card">
      <div class="rank-header">
        <h2 class="rank-title">12. 4th and 10 — Basco</h2>
        <span class="projection-badge">PROJ: 118.8 PTS</span>
      </div>
      <div class="player-roster">Jayden Daniels • James Cook • Ladd McConkey • Waddle • Montgomery</div>
      <p class="rank-analysis">Basco brings years of fantasy football experience to the table. There's just one problem: zero playoff experience.</p>
      <p class="rank-analysis">He's mastered fantasy football. He just hasn't mastered making the postseason.</p>
      <div class="verdict">Verdict: Rebuilding Mode.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="special-section">
      <h2>🔥 Bold Predictions</h2>
      <ul class="predictions-list">
        <li>Michael finishes with the league's best regular-season record.</li>
        <li>Phil makes a deep playoff run and reminds everyone about his résumé.</li>
        <li>Drew gets formally accused of cheating before Week 5.</li>
        <li>Frank executes at least one trade that makes the entire league ask, “WHY?”</li>
        <li>Donovan drops a close game and turns the group chat into an active war zone.</li>
        <li>Levi still hasn't worked up the courage to tell Phil how he feels.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="special-section" style="background: #111;">
      <h2>🏆 Preseason Awards</h2>
      <ul class="awards-list">
        <li><span class="award-name">MVP</span><span class="award-winner">Amon-Ra St. Brown</span></li>
        <li><span class="award-name">Biggest Sleeper</span><span class="award-winner">Drewbacca</span></li>
        <li><span class="award-name">Biggest Disappointment</span><span class="award-winner">Cooking Up Wins</span></li>
        <li><span class="award-name">Worst Trade Incoming</span><span class="award-winner">Frank</span></li>
        <li><span class="award-name">Most Likely to Rage</span><span class="award-winner">Donovan</span></li>
        <li><span class="award-name">Most Likely to Be Investigated</span><span class="award-winner">Drew</span></li>
        <li><span class="award-name">Most Likely to Confess Feelings</span><span class="award-winner">Levi</span></li>
        <li><span class="award-name">Best Golfer / Worst Threat</span><span class="award-winner">Darek</span></li>
        <li><span class="award-name">Miss Lineup Due to Baby</span><span class="award-winner">Reese</span></li>
        <li><span class="award-name">In Need of Audio Description</span><span class="award-winner">Gordies</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="final-call">
      <h2>🎙️ Final Call</h2>
      <p>Twelve managers. Twelve rosters. Twelve completely different levels of confidence.</p>
      <p>Some think they're destined for a championship. Some think their draft was genius. And some are about to discover that fantasy football is significantly harder when everyone else is trying too.</p>
      <p class="final-date">SEPTEMBER 9, 2026.</p>
      <p><strong>The excuses end. The lineups lock. The trash talk begins.</strong></p>
      <p style="margin-top: 10px; font-weight: 800; color: #111;">One manager will lift the trophy.</p>
    </div>
